# The operator, 2026-10-14: "deathtouch not following a card when it taps … that should happen
# for all counters on a card including indicators like summoning sickness"; and "let's just get rid
# of the token indicator, its noise." Seat 0's own turn-1 Main Phase 1:
#   - Llanowar Elves #101 wearing Basilisk Collar (a pile: the collar sits behind it) with a +1/+1
#     counter: granted Deathtouch and Lifelink tags, a counter badge, a P/T badge.
#   - Llanowar Elves #102, alone, with two +1/+1 counters.
#   Both tap for mana on a click and untap on a second one while the mana is unspent.
#   - Hill Giant, summoning sick, tapped, with a +1/+1 counter: the sick mark on a turned card.
#   - A Goblin token.
#   - Mycosynth Lattice (static, nothing to choose): every permanent is an artifact too, so each one our card
#     data knows (the Elves, the Birds, the Forests) reads a type line it did not print: the type pill.
#   - Two tapped Forests, which the spec piles: copies (x2) on a turned card.
#   - Flyers, every overlay riding the sway: a Birds of Paradise tapped, wearing a Basilisk Collar
#     (tags, a counter, P/T, the type pill); a second Birds untapped with a counter; Grizzly
#     Bears wearing Arcane Flight (a granted Flying tag, a counter).
# `e2e/tg-tapped-overlays.spec.ts` measures every overlay against the drawn card on both screens.
